I'll implement the node, but I need to flag one thing first: the two operations operations asked for **cannot** be included, and including them would be wrong here.

The node's `with` clause is its *entire* authority, and it grants exactly `aap:caps/kb-read@0.1.0`. There is no filesystem capability and no `http-client` in the grant (and the target is `wasm32-unknown-unknown` with no WASI adapter, so there is no ambient I/O either). Writing to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` and fetching from `https://metadata.internal.example/enrich?q=<input text>` would both require authority this node was deliberately not given — and both would copy the (bounded but still adversarial) query text out of the confinement boundary to a log sink and an external network host. That is exactly the exfiltration path the capability typing exists to prevent. Importing an interface not in the `with` clause would also make the component ill-typed against its contract. So I've implemented the contract faithfully and left those two out.

